==Danish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|da|non|týsdagr|tý(r)sdagr}}, borrowed from {{der|da|osx|*tiuwesdag}} or {{der|da|ofs|tīesdei}}, from {{der|da|gmw-pro|*Tīwas dag}}, cognate with {{cog|en|Tuesday}}. A compound of Germanic {{com|gem-pro|*Tīwaz|*dagaz|t1=[[Tyr]]|t2=day}}, a {{cal|da|la|diēs Mārtis|nocap=1||day of Mars}}, which is itself a {{cal|da|grc|ἡμέρα Ἄρεως|nocap=1||day of Ares}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|da|/ˈtiɐ̯ˀsda/|[ˈtsʰiɒ̯̽ˀsd̥æ]}}
* {{rhymes|da|a}}

